exports[`the worked example renders the approved markdown structure > agent skin 1`] = `
"# Brightwater support desk — peak staffing

## Framing

### Goals \`purpose\`

- **Decide peak staffing** — stated · confirmed \`e1\`

## Scope

### Horizons \`horizon\`

- **Weekday morning peak** — stated · confirmed \`e7\`
  - The measure is average waiting time from joining the queue to answer, over the peak window, reported weekly. — stated · confirmed \`c1\`
  - Six agents are on today's weekday morning peak block. — stated · confirmed \`c3\`
  - The phone-system export shows about 50 calls an hour in the peak, arriving unevenly; off-peak is closer to 15. — evidenced · confirmed \`c5\`
    - ~~About 45 calls an hour arrive during the peak.~~ — superseded \`c4\`
  - Is there a pattern inside the two-hour block beyond “it builds after ten”? — stated · open \`c11\`

## Inputs

### Levers \`lever\`

- **Agents on the block** — stated · confirmed \`e4\`
  - Staffing is a whole number of agents from two to eight; eight seats and licences is the cap, two is the floor the team leads will accept. — stated · confirmed \`c2\`
  - Is the current six one agent too many on the peak block? — stated · conflicted \`c10\`

### Limits \`limit\`

- **Seat and licence cap** — stated · confirmed \`e5\`
  - Staffing is a whole number of agents from two to eight; eight seats and licences is the cap, two is the floor the team leads will accept. — stated · confirmed \`c2\`

## The system

### Items \`thing\`

- **Callers** — stated · confirmed \`e8\`
  - The phone-system export shows about 50 calls an hour in the peak, arriving unevenly; off-peak is closer to 15. — evidenced · confirmed \`c5\`
    - ~~About 45 calls an hour arrive during the peak.~~ — superseded \`c4\`
  - Calls come in at random around the rate and handle times vary around six minutes — the team's working assumption, not something measured. — assumed · tentative \`c7\`
  - Is there a pattern inside the two-hour block beyond “it builds after ten”? — stated · open \`c11\`

### Locations \`location\`

- **The queue** — stated · confirmed \`e9\`
  - Callers start hanging up after about eight to ten minutes on hold; the export shows when they left, not why. — stated · tentative \`c9\`

### Resources \`resource\`

- **Agents on the phones** — stated · confirmed \`e10\`
  - Six agents are on today's weekday morning peak block. — stated · confirmed \`c3\`
  - Is the current six one agent too many on the peak block? — stated · conflicted \`c10\`

### Activities \`activity\`

- **Call handling** — stated · confirmed \`e11\`
  - Average handle time is about six minutes with plenty of spread: under two minutes for bill queries, past fifteen for complaints. — evidenced · confirmed \`c6\`
  - Calls come in at random around the rate and handle times vary around six minutes — the team's working assumption, not something measured. — assumed · tentative \`c7\`

### Events \`event\`

- **Caller abandonment** — stated · tentative \`e12\`
  - Callers start hanging up after about eight to ten minutes on hold; the export shows when they left, not why. — stated · tentative \`c9\`

## Outputs

### Metrics \`metric\`

- **Average waiting time** — stated · confirmed \`e2\`
  - The measure is average waiting time from joining the queue to answer, over the peak window, reported weekly. — stated · confirmed \`c1\`

### Maximizations / Minimizations \`direction\`

- **Keep peak waiting time low** — stated · confirmed \`e3\`

### Thresholds \`threshold\`

- **The ten-minute promise** — stated · confirmed \`e6\`
  - No caller waits more than ten minutes — a hard rule, not a preference to trade off. — stated · confirmed \`c8\`

## Open questions

:::question
Is the current six one agent too many on the peak block?

Accounts disagree and nobody has said which holds. Concerns: Agents on the block, Agents on the phones. Record: c10.

- [ ] It holds
- [ ] It does not hold
- [ ] Leave it unresolved
:::

:::question
Is there a pattern inside the two-hour block beyond “it builds after ten”?

It matters and nobody knows yet. Concerns: Weekday morning peak, Callers. Record: c11.
:::

## Excluded from the model

- **Cost of an agent-hour** — metric · stated · out-of-scope \`e13\`
  - Cost stays out of the comparison; the decision is made on waiting time within two to eight agents. — stated · confirmed \`c12\`"
`;

